releaseNotes:
v3.1 - Added three commands for moving a large estate out of TFVC into a handful of git repos, all sharing one solution discovery layer that reads .sln and .slnx files in-process rather than shelling out to 'dotnet sln list' (which cannot see Web Site projects or project type GUIDs and needs an SDK installed); survey: a read-only scan that counts the things that hurt during or after the migration -- Web Site projects, non-SDK projects, checked-in packages and build output, TFVC and VSS source control bindings, unbuildable project types (.vbp/.vdproj/.wdproj), signing keys, config files with inline passwords, paths over 200 characters, names that differ only by case, files over 50 MB and projects copied to more than one path -- with --output to write a CSV of every hit. The password value itself is never printed; mergesolutions: finds every solution and writes one Everything.slnx referencing every project once, filed into a solution folder per component, so that MSBuild builds one project graph instead of N solutions one after another. --filters also writes a .slnf per component; generatepipelines: writes Azure DevOps build.yml plus a templates/build-solution.yml jobs template, in 'single' mode (one job building the merged solution) or 'jobs' mode (one job per discovered solution). Picks msbuild over dotnet automatically when a solution holds a non-SDK-style or database project, and only overwrites files it generated itself;
v3.0.1 - findsolutions: fixed the --json option. The command handed the analysis objects to the serializer directly and those hold FileInfo and DirectoryInfo values. DirectoryInfo exposes Parent and Root as more DirectoryInfo instances and a root directory is its own Root, so the serializer walked that chain until it reported an object cycle. Every property it touched on the way was a filesystem call, which is why it ran for a long time before failing. Results are now projected onto plain classes that hold paths as strings; findsolutions: --json is no longer ignored when --listprojects is not supplied; findsolutions: fixed the table output for a project that has no references. The row was built with the twelve CSV columns no matter which format was being written, so the table formatter rejected it with "Expected 5 columns but received 12 columns". With --skipreferences this affected every project, so that combination could never run;
v3.0 - BREAKING. Upgraded to Benday.CommandsFramework v5. slnutil now returns a real exit code: a failed command exits 1 rather than the 0 that every run reported before, so a script or pipeline step that runs slnutil will start seeing failures it previously ignored; Arguments are now typed in the POSIX long option form -- '--name value', '--name=value', '--name:value' and '--flag' -- which is what usage output, shell completion and validation messages render. The original '/name:value' form still parses and prints a deprecation warning on stderr; Unknown arguments are now a validation failure rather than being ignored, so a misspelled argument name stops the command instead of silently going missing; Added the 'tui' terminal interface -- run 'slnutil tui' to browse the commands, fill in a form, copy the command line it adds up to, and run it; runsql now enforces 'exactly one of sqlcommand or sqlfile' as a declared argument rule, so the requirement appears in usage output and in the --json schema; The --json schema is now an object with SchemaVersion rather than a bare array of commands; createsolution's 'commands' template now generates a v5 tool;
v2.41.1 - findsolutions: fixed cross-solution reference detection. Relative paths written with backslashes were not resolved when running on macOS or Linux, and containment was compared without a directory boundary so a sibling folder sharing a name prefix read as being inside its neighbour. Both made outside-of-solution-root report false when it should have reported true;
v2.41 - Refactored FindSolutions command to default to table formatted output when list projects is requested;
v2.40 - enablecodeanalysis: also installs Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.CodeStyle for IDE rule enforcement (default on; opt out with /enforce-code-style:false); added /codestyle-version to pin the package version;
v2.39 - findsolutions: added target-framework and uses-packages-config columns plus finer-grained reference-type classification (framework-ref, nuget-via-packages-config, fixed PackageReference detection); Added enablecodeanalysis command to streamline VS2026 code
   analysis across a solution, with a per-project mode for packages.config solutions;
v2.38 - Fixing bugs in findsolutions command; Updating createsolution to create modern xunit projects;
v2.37 - Added updategithubactionsversions command to update GitHub Actions versions in workflow files;
v2.36 - Added formatjson command to format JSON files;
v2.35 - Added 'gui' support to launch a blazor UI for this command; Updated dependencies and minor bug fixes;
v2.34 - Modified find solutions command to also find .slnx files;
v2.33 - Modified SetJsonValueCommand to allow incrementing patch version numbers;
v2.32.1 - Updated dependencies to fix security vulnerabilities;
v2.32 - Added support for .net10; Added support for slnx files; Modified create solution command to no longer install FluentAssertions library;
v2.31 - Modified classes from json command to 1) detect DateTime property values 2) optionally generate inner classes instead of separate classes;
v2.30 - Added clipboard option to classes from json command to read JSON from clipboard instead of a file or console input;
v2.29 - Added printfile command to read a text file and print it to the console character by character. This is helpful for diagnosing encoding issues and weird text issues.;
v2.28 - Adding run sql command to execute SQL commands or SQL script files against a SQL Server database;
v2.27 - Adding support for json comments to JsonToClasses command;
v2.26 - Added command to sort references in a csproj file.
v2.25 - Added utility to check versions in bicep files and update to latest.
v2.24 - Added option to devtreeclean to preserve node_modules directories.
v2.23 - Added command to sort the values in the first PropertyGroup of a csproj file; Fixing bugs related to Process.Start() timeouts and stream reading in CreateSolutionCommand.
v2.22 - Added set package version command to update NuGet package versions in project files using optional package name filtering.
v2.21 - Modified set framework version command to more gracefully handle OS-specific targeting. Adding net8.0 and net9.0 to target frameworks.
v2.20 - Added prefix option to bulk rename command
v2.19 - Bug fixes; Support in class diagram for protected members; Class diagram option for showing locally defined members
v2.18 - Fixing bugs in formatxml command
v2.17 - Fixing bugs in class diagram generator
v2.16 - Restored the devtreeclean command which had been accidentally removed.
